WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.880
[Beats x3]

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.940
Did you see the teaser for Deadpool 2 that came out, before Logan?

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.720
It was a perfect, Deadpool story, hilarious, shocking and er..

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.860
Wait a minute

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.020
How did he eat that ice cream, he doesn't have a spoon?

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.040
You can break the fourth wall all you want, Wade.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:20.480
But don't you for a second try to tell me you eat your ice cream spoon-less.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.400
Unless...

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.720
[Overlay] there is no spoon

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.020
There's no spoon! Deadpool exists within the matrix.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.420
I call this one

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.700
THEORY CONFIRMED!

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:46.020
[Intro Music]

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.420
Hello Internet, and welcome to Film Theory

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.820
The show that is so poor we don't even have a fourth wall to break.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.960
This week I am revisiting Deadpool, because

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.080
if I am being 100% honest, I couldn't for the life of me think of any good theories for Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.920
Seriously! I love that movie. I just had like writers blocked or something. Groot's speech impediment, that's

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:12.480
Kinda boring. Uhh, who's Peter dad, which is going to get revealed in Guardians 2, like science of

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.600
rocket raccoon...that's not fun either.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.440
Anyways, if you have any good idea for guardians, let me know down in the comments. I want to do a video on the franchise so bad

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:28.020
But hey, you know what that's okay because it gives me an excuse to spend a little bit more quality time with everyone favorite merc with a mouth

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.180
Wade Wilson

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.040
Last year Deadpool movie gave us all the violent comedy that we could ask for

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:40.040
But despite all the cool action scenes, holiday themed sexy time, the thing everyone loves about this character is his metaness.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.520
The fact that he talks to us.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:48.120
[Wade fucking Wilson] Fourth wall break inside a fourth wall break that's like 16 walls.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.620
He is like the super hero equivalent to a YouTube vlogger.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:56.000
All he needs to do is ask for people to Subscribe and get himself a LootCrate sponsorship and he has made it

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:56.820
Liza Koshy

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.340
You watch your back, Deadpool's coming for ya!

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.080
Now, during the film he breaks the 4th wall exactly 23 times

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.940
To make sure that we're having a good time

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.940
But what I'm out to prove today is that

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:10.200
Deadpool's most meta joke is the ultimate of wall breaks

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.340
A 24th, wink at the camera that skirted under all of our collective radars

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:20.480
A move so brilliant, so subversive, and so purely Deadpool

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.640
That it can only be accomplished in a movie like this one

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.420
So my loyal theorists, today I ask you to consider the following

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.340
Did Deadpool, write Deadpool?

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.900
Obviously the movie had real writers credited to Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.280
But did they write the movie to be as though Deadpool

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.500
Wrote the movie

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.480
Creating a script that is in it of itself a 4th wall break

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.620
A script written by it's own character about himself starring himself

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.500
it's a premise that seems absurd

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:52.900
But then again, absurdity is exactly what this movie, and its character

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:53.860
Are all about

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.360
Let's start at the beginning

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.160
Deadpool is clearly aware of his role as a movie character

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.480
And the film in general

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:00.600
And as we see in the opening moment

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.160
He's really pleased to finally have a movie all of his own

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.400
[Deadpool] Who's balls did I have to fondle to get my own movie?

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.640
But that's not always the case

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.500
In fact, Deadpool has a...

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.780
Difficult history

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.540
With adaptation of his story

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.500
As an example

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.980
Let's look at Deadpool video game from back in 2013

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.560
The opening scene of the game

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.800
Shows us Deadpool on a phone with the game developer

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.980
Talking about an idea that he pitched to them

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:24.900
His name for it,

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.000
The most awesome game ever

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.740
But when High Moon Studio refused to greenlight that pitch

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.680
He rigs their studio with explosives and forces them to make the game for him

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:45.820
Fast forward a bit and we see that Deadpool is worried about of all things

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.180
The script

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.100
And when he finally gets his script delivered to his door

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.080
He ABSOLUTELY hates it

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.100
So

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.380
He takes it upon himself to rewrite the whole thing in crayon

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.000
And he doesn't just stop at the script

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.700
We watch as he call up voice actor

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:08.440
Nolan North

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.820
and hires him for the job of playing himself

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.020
In the game that we in that moment are playing

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:21.900
So writers of Deadpool's stories have clearly shown a history of his character

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.040
Hijacking productions about himself and rewriting them

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.360
But that's not all

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:27.440
In the comics

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.420
Deadpool has never been shy about talking directly to the

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:31.960
writer or artist of any given issue

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:32.820
Take for instance

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.220
Deadpool Volume 1 where he address creator Rob Liefeld directly

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.740
So why does he never do that in the movie?

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:43.120
Sure he moves the camera to force the audience to look away from him torturing "Agent Smith"

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.760
But other than that he never directly interacts with the people making the film

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.660
Director, sound guy, or writer

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.760
Instead he only complains about the studio

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.640
The one's paying for the movie

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.800
Doing things like complaining that the studio was too cheap to get more than two X-Men for their film

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.140
But as for the creative team

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:03.240
Outside of getting ripped on the opening credits he leaves them completely alone

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.500
Which is a strange  decision for a character who does this literally

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.220
ALL THE TIME

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.880
in all his other incarnations

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.820
Even in moments when that team supposedly screws up

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.860
*awkward fapping*

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.780
Lets focus on this moment for a second think about it this way

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.900
His 4th wall breaks don't stop the action of the movie

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:25.680
In his opening monologue, we see cars driving pass him as he sits on the edge of the highway addressing us

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:32.540
He even mentions directly to Colossus a few minutes later that these 4th wall breaks are specifically for our benefit

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.240
These moment show us that outside of the flash backs

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:39.180
The 4th wall breaks are happening in the moment

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:43.080
In real time, when he adjust the camera before of his torture of "Agent Smith"

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.960
Smith look directly at the camera before it turns away

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:52.180
This proofs that Deadpool is manipulating the 4th wall in these moments as they're being filmed

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.440
As they happened

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.880
Not after the fact or pausing the action to step out of the events of the movie

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.160
And yet, when he's caught having special time with his unicorn

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.840
He doesn't yell or complain to the editors or the director that they're filming this

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.960
In fact, he knows it's being left in the final product of the movie

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:11.880
Acknowledging this was a part that we weren't meant to see

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.280
But that we're seeing it anyway

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:18.480
But if he's adhering to the rules of his 4th wall breaks as it's been established as they're happening in real time

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.920
He wouldn't know this was being left in the final cut

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.660
So, long story short

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:28.580
Even thou Deadpool says we weren't meant to see it the fact that he comments on the fact we weren't meant to see it

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.460
Shows that he knows that we're seeing it

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.560
And that he has approved that the fact we are seeing it

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.380
Thus, he's in control of how this story is being told

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:35.880
*mind blown*

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.900
WHoOoOohohoho

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:38.940
You got all that?

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.740
Ohh it's like a logic puzzle!

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:44.740
I think I..just felt my brain melt through my ear carnal

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:49.320
Alright, so this is the Deadpool origin story as Deadpool would want us to see it

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.100
Clearly he would wanna make himself look as good as possible right?

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:55.380
Right! and that's exactly what he does

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.160
In the comics, Deadpool's history often left vague

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:01.600
The main thing about his origin always tend to remain constant though are

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.060
A. he's a mercenary before his mutation

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.400
B. he's Canadian

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:08.820
And C. his superpower comes from Wolverine's blood

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:13.320
Now, Deadpool references Wolverine and Hugh Jackman multiple times throughout the movie

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:13.860
BUTT

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:16.200
The movie never mentioned any other mutant

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:21.160
Wolverine or otherwise having anything to do with Deadpool's mutation

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:24.280
In this version of events, the mutation was inside him all along

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.400
It's unlocked through lots of torture

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.720
This makes Deadpool the star of his own story

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:34.760
And not some background character who got his powers riding the coattail some other mutant

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:40.860
It makes Deadpool inherently special rather than having to get his specialness bestowed upon him

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:42.220
By someone else

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:45.540
Speaking of those mutation in both the comics and the film

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.540
Deadpool's only true mutation is the ability to heal wounds really fast

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:52.020
Doing things like cutting off and regrowing his hand *BABY HAAAANDS!!!*

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:55.080
But, other than that he's a completely normal human being

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.700
Which makes some of the things he does in the film a bit far-fetched

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.900
Even by comic book movies standards

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:03.000
Sure, they reference his special forces training

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.320
But for as stellar as spec-ops training maybe

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:10.100
I doubt it gives someone the ability to line up a triple headshot while flipping through the air

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:13.060
Soldiers tend to keep their feet on the ground whenever possible

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:14.700
They ain't training you to be an acrobat

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.880
Also for taking the film at face value Deadpool would be at fluent at soccer

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:18.580
Firing blind

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.760
Sword throwing

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.740
In the comics Deadpool was able to do thing like this by using his 4th wall breaking

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:28.440
He reads ahead, jumps between panels, allowing him to do cool stunts and moves like these

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:33.280
But the film version of Deadpool never uses the 4th wall breaking for his own advantage

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:39.240
When in combat he remains within the world of the film even if he occasionally strikes a silly pose mid flight

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.780
So where did the cirque du soleil murder ability come from?

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:45.180
Our only option is that, whoever wrote this

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:49.260
Really wanted Deadpool to come off looking as cool as possible in the final film

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.940
Even if he might not really have those abilities based on his mutation

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:58.720
And who would wanna make Deadpool looked like the coolest superhero of all time more than Deadpool himself

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:00.060
From around the subject of looking good

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.680
Wade Wilson REALLY cares about his appearance

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.540
So much so that he completely avoids talking to the love of his life

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.020
Simply because he turn into the human equivalent to the California raisin

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.660
Deadpool clearly loves the look of Ryan Renolds almost as much as he loves stuffed unicorns

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.580
And if Deadpool choose any actor to play him, it would be Ryan

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.520
We know this because he thought of himself this way for years

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.880
In Cable &amp; Deadpool volume 1 number 2, Deadpool refers to himself as quote

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.160
"Ryan Renolds crossed with a shar-pei"

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:36.800
And if you think that's just tongue and cheek movie references is worth noting that this issue was from 2004

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:41.160
5 years before Ryan Renolds played Deadpool in X-Men Origins

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:45.640
And more than a decade before Ryan Renolds play Deadpool in the good Deadpool movie

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:52.180
And remember how in the game we saw Deadpool cast Nolan North for his voice

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:57.600
Well, in a film, it'd be total wish fulfillment for Deadpool the character to cast the role of himself

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.740
As the world sexiest Canadian

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:04.120
However, the part of the film that feels most like Deadpool's writer wish fulfillment

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.020
Is Wade's relationship with Vanessa

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:10.320
She does appears in the comics, but her story is completely different there

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:13.320
The big difference is that they never get back together

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.020
I'm not kidding!

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:18.740
Deadpool's epic quest to reclaim his lost love is completely unique to the film

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:21.200
In the comic, she's discovered to be a shapeshifting mutant

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.540
Who also become a mercenary after he leaves her

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:29.500
In the film, this relationship is changed from the brief fling, to a love story for the ages

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:32.800
Complete with the perfect Hollywood ending

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.220
And as we see throughout Deadpool

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:40.420
Wade, just love himself some romantic movie cheese

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:44.760
*reference no. 1*

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.020
*aaaaand another reference*

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:52.740
Even the physics of the movie is rewritten so that Deadpool can gives himself his desired happy ending

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:56.680
Ajax has Vanessa in a suffocation chamber made out of glass and metal

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:02.320
Now earlier in the movie we saw Wade Wilson escape an identical chamber by launching it across the room with an explosion

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.900
Which, as you see here shattered the glass

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:08.680
And yet, when Vanessa is in the exact replica of that chamber

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:14.120
She falls of an aircraft carrier and gets buried in huge slabs of concrete

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:18.620
All after Deadpool has already crack the glass to help her breath

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.760
So, of course, she emerges without a scratch on her *sarcasm*

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:22.680
WHAT?

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:23.760
COME ON!

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.280
Look at the size of that concrete slab!

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.220
As much as I love doing unnecessary math on this show

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.840
I don't think I need to crunch any numbers to know that

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:35.180
That glass is not gonna be in one piece when she hits the ground

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:39.420
And I'm not even gonna address the fact that Vanessa survived the fall to begin with

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:44.300
More convenient rewrite by the guy in the red and black spandex

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.980
At this point you might be thinking to yourself

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.640
Hang on Matt Patt, this is all possible

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.300
But it can also be a load of confirmation bias

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:52.680
And yeah, you're right

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.920
ABSOLUTELY RIGHT!

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:59.480
But there is one last minor detail that I think brings it all together

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:03.540
When "Agent Smith" shows up to recruit Deadpool for the superhero creation program

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:06.200
Just listen to what Wade's best buddy Weasel says

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.140
"That guy over there came in looking for you"

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:11.700
"little Grim Reaper type I don't know...might further the "PLOT"

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:12.960
But, hold on

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.080
Since when can he break the 4th wall?

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:18.560
Until this very moment, no one else seems aware that they're in a movie

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:21.160
The only way this line makes any sort of senses

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:26.460
is if Weasel knows that "Agent Smith is there to literally further a movie's plot

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:28.400
No one would naturally say this

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:33.900
But it is the sort of logical inconsistency that Deadpool himself would write into a script

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:37.320
And that brings us all the way back around to the opening credit of the film

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:41.360
Each crew and cast member gets themselves a sarcastic description

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.440
Directed by an overpaid tool, produced by asshats

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:48.380
Starring a hot chick, a CGI character, a gratuitous cameo

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:53.580
Of all the titles, the only complimentary ones are for Deadpool himself

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.860
As God's perfect idiot

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.840
And you guess it, the writers

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:59.120
AKA the real heroes

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:04.020
Could it be that Wade Wilson is trying to slip us a little hint as that who he thinks is really to thank

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.820
For the spectacle you're about to see

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.940
But hey, that's just a theory

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.100
A FILM THEORY!

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:12.920
Aaaaaaaaand

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:13.720
CUT!

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.720
*enter some kind of I don't know type of music*

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:20.400
*it's like a fucking carnival music type of shit*

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.100
*Oh God how long will this music last...*

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:29.760
*please send help*

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.980
*aaaaaaand it's done! finally!*

